WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:04.740
PIOTR STEINKILLER: Welcome.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.320
I'm Piotr Steinkeller.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.380
I teach Assyriology and Ancient
Mesopotamian history and Religion

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.760
at Harvard.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.170
And today I would like to share
with you a very special cuneiform

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.610
tablet which belongs to the collection
of the Harvard Semitic Museum.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:28.400
It is one of the most important
cuneiform tablets in our collection.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:38.030
It dates roughly to 1,700 BCE, the
reign of the great Hammurabi of Babylon.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.900
It is written in the Akkadian language.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.340
What makes this tablet so unique--

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.100
it is a manual of the divination.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.600
a priest called baru, in Akkadian--

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.920
another term from him is haruspex--

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.280
and he was a specialist,
ritual specialist,

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:05.720
who foretold future from the
appearance of sheep's intestines.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:12.710
The tablet contains 142 lines.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:15.890
This is what we call the
frontside, or the obverse.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.290
OK, so this is the beginning
of the tablet here.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.910
I would like to point out that the
scribe is incredibly small and tiny.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:28.140
It's quite unusual in that way.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:34.340
So we have probably something like 60
lines over the front or the obverse,

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.650
and then the tablet
continues on the back.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:42.200
The reverse of the tablet, up to here.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.590
The manual tells the diviner
what he may find in the exta,

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.745
and how he should honorize the exta.

00:01:49.745 --> 00:01:55.170
The text begins with ritual
instructions for the diviner, which

00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:00.690
instruct him how he should
invite the gods to the extispicy.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.140
And the central figure
here is the sun god.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:15.120
And how he may ask the gods to obtain
a favorable answer to his query.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:21.180
So he should offer offerings,
prepare offerings, say some prayers,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.170
and then he should sacrifice a sheep.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:32.000
Having slaughtered the sheep, he then
should ask the sun god and other gods

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.340
for a positive answer.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.300
And they are supposed to inscribe
the answer in the entrails

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.750
of the sacrificial sheep.

